</div>
</div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float">Prompt 2 </span>For geospatial knowledge (box) baseline, where the input is a location name and the output is predicted bounding box.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For approaches introduced in §<a href="#S4" title="4 Geocoding Complex Location References ‣ Coordinates from Context: Using LLMs to Ground Complex Location References" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> for geocoding complex location references, we use Prompt <a href="#lstfloat3" title="Prompt 3 ‣ Appendix A Additional Experimental Details ‣ Coordinates from Context: Using LLMs to Ground Complex Location References" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> for the Geoparser-augmented <span id="A1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">reasoner</span> and Prompt <a href="#lstfloat4" title="Prompt 4 ‣ Appendix A Additional Experimental Details ‣ Coordinates from Context: Using LLMs to Ground Complex Location References" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> for the Direct <span id="A1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">reasoner</span>.
For the End-to-end LLM approach, we use Prompt <a href="#lstfloat5" title="Prompt 5 ‣ Appendix A Additional Experimental Details ‣ Coordinates from Context: Using LLMs to Ground Complex Location References" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> for the <span id="A1.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">recaller</span> and Prompt <a href="#lstfloat3" title="Prompt 3 ‣ Appendix A Additional Experimental Details ‣ Coordinates from Context: Using LLMs to Ground Complex Location References" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> for the <span id="A1.p6.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">reasoner</span>.
When evaluating fine-tuned models, the examples in system prompts were excluded.</p>
</div>
